<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39119" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prōtector</span></b> , ōris,
			m.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen., <i>a coverer;</i> trop., <i>a
			protector</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">legum protectores,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Apol. 6</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Psa. 17,
			3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			In partic., <i>one of the lifeguard</i> or <i>body - guard</i> (post - class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inter protectores suos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Spart. Carac. 7</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Amm. 14, 7, 9</span></i>; Cod. Th. 6, 24;
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Grut. 1028, 2 al.</span></i>
			
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
